{"title":"HelioVet","sub":"Entering Poland: go direct or use a distributor?","type":"Market entry","industry":"Veterinary software","geo":"Poland","diff":2,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Entry mode · ramp-up · partner economics","prompt":"HelioVet, a German company, sells software that stores and analyses X-ray images for veterinary clinics, at $150 per clinic per month. After success at home it wants to enter Poland. Localisation and certification would cost $400k up front. The CEO asks: is Poland worth entering, and should HelioVet build its own sales team or work through a distributor?","clarify":[{"q":"Which clinics can use it?","a":"Only clinics with digital X-ray: about 35% of Poland's 4,800 clinics today, and rising."},{"q":"Distribution?","a":"Two specialist distributors sell equipment to most Polish clinics. One has offered to resell HelioVet for 25% of revenue."},{"q":"Costs?","a":"Support costs about $30 per clinic per month. A direct team (sales, support, Polish-speaking staff) would cost $350k a year; with the distributor, $150k."},{"q":"Objective?","a":"Recover the entry investment within four years."}],"structure":{"root":"Should HelioVet enter Poland, and how?","branches":[{"head":"Market","items":["Clinics with digital X-ray","Growth in digital adoption","Competing software"]},{"head":"Economics per clinic","items":["Price, support cost","Distributor's share"]},{"head":"Entry mode","items":["Direct: cost and speed of ramp-up","Distributor: margin given up vs reach"]}]},"hypothesis":"The market is small, so speed of adoption matters more than margin. A distributor that already visits most clinics could win customers much faster.","questions":[{"q":"How big is the addressable market today?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<p>Addressable: 4,800 × 35% = <b>1,680 clinics</b>.</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> a small market, so any plan will need a large share of it, and the speed of winning clinics will matter.</p>"},{"q":"Here are the two ramp-up plans. Compare cumulative profit over four years, after the $400k investment.","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"400.538pt\" height=\"185.46pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 400.538 185.46\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 185.46 L 400.538 185.46 L 400.538 -0 L 0 -0 L 0 185.46 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 47.378 160.352 L 393.338 160.352 L 393.338 27.296 L 47.378 27.296 L 47.378 160.352 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"matplotlib.axis_1\"><g id=\"xtick_1\"><g id=\"line2d_1\"><defs><path id=\"mff7d576334\" d=\"M 0 0 L 0 3.5 \" style=\"stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></defs><g><use xlink:href=\"#mff7d576334\" x=\"96.209675\" y=\"160.352\" style=\"fill: #555555; stroke: #555555; stroke-width: 0.8\"/></g></g><g id=\"text_1\"><g style=\"fill: #555555\" transform=\"translate(83.789675 176.046) scale(0.09 -0.09)\"><defs><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-38\" d=\"M 3994 4749 Q 4038 4749 4054 4723 Q 4070 4698 4045 4659 L 2522 2112 Q 2496 2074 2489 2035 Q 2483 1997 2483 1901 L 2483 109 Q 2483 0 2362 0 L 1978 0 Q 1914 0 1894 25 Q 1875 51 1875 96 L 1875 1875 Q 1875 1939 1862 1971 Q 1850 2003 1824 2048 L 282 4646 Q 256 4691 272 4720 Q 288 4749 352 4749 L 813 4749 Q 870 4749 896 4733 Q 922 4717 947 4672 L 2138 2624 Q 2176 2554 2208 2550 Q 2240 2547 2278 2611 L 3462 4672 Q 3488 4723 3513 4736 Q 3539 4749 3597 4749 L 3994 4749 L 3994 4749 z\n\" transform=\"scale(0.015625)\"/><path id=\"LibreFranklin-Regular-48\" d=\"M 851 1485 Q 851 1171 1001 912 Q 1152 653 1405 499 Q 1658 346 1971 346 Q 2291 346 2540 477 Q 2790 608 2970 877 Q 2995 902 3011 905 Q 3027 909 3059 896 L 3328 762 Q 3386 730 3341 672 Q 3168 416 2960 253 Q 2752 90 2496 13 Q 2240 -64 1920 -64 Q 1446 -64 1081 153 Q 717 371 505 761 Q 294 1152 294 1664 Q 294 2221